WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.998
This is Neural Voices.

2
00:00:02.194 --> 00:00:06.896
It reads web pages aloud, with a natural voice that runs inside your browser.

3
00:00:08.772 --> 00:00:11.212
Long articles are tiring to read on a screen.

4
00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:15.944
Good reading voices usually cost money, or send your text to someone else's computer.

5
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.369
This one does neither.

6
00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:23.666
Select some text and click the speaker, or press play to read the whole article.

7
00:00:23.832 --> 00:00:28.662
The sentence is shaded, and the word being spoken is marked, so you can follow along.

8
00:00:30.508 --> 00:00:31.867
It knows the language.

9
00:00:32.047 --> 00:00:37.804
English and Swedish are recognised paragraph by paragraph, so a mixed page switches voice by itself.

10
00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:40.780
Och när texten är på svenska, läser Alma den.

11
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.756
You keep a short list of the voices you like, and pick a default voice for each language.

12
00:00:46.872 --> 00:00:50.483
There are a hundred and seventy voices in forty nine languages to choose from.

13
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:57.169
Speed is changed inside the voice, so it sounds natural from slow to twice as fast.

14
00:00:57.354 --> 00:01:02.857
When you stop, it uses no processor time, and it frees its memory after a few quiet minutes.

15
00:01:04.721 --> 00:01:06.964
Everything happens on your computer.

16
00:01:07.163 --> 00:01:11.731
The only thing it downloads is a voice, once, the first time you use it.

17
00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:17.799
Every voice has its own licence, and the settings page shows it.

18
00:01:18.016 --> 00:01:21.104
I am Cori, made from public domain recordings.

19
00:01:21.321 --> 00:01:26.000
The Swedish voice, Alma, is shared under Creative Commons Attribution.

20
00:01:27.897 --> 00:01:34.785
Neural Voices is built on Piper, ONNX Runtime and espeak N G, and this video is narrated by the add-on itself.

21
00:01:36.669 --> 00:01:38.216
The code is free on GitHub.

22
00:01:38.377 --> 00:01:41.476
Load it in Firefox or Chromium, and let it read to you.

